                <pb facs="0597" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.4016/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-02T17:00:00+01:00">September 2, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 2—2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>225. My telegram No. 223, September 1, 6 p.m. The Council of Ministers today
                    approved a Decree Law excluding all persons both of whose parents were of the
                    Jewish race from the teaching profession in general and barring such persons
                    from admission to all schools and institutions of learning recognized by the
                    State. A transitional exception is made in the cases of those previously
                    enrolled in the universities who will be permitted to continue their
                    studies.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
